Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|true|
		|portal.upstream|true|
		|testray.main.component.name|Elastic Search Impl|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG

Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given PortalInstances tear Down CP
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: Assert Config File Values Propogate To Module
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|osgi.module.configuration.file.names|com.liferay.portal.search.elasticsearch.configuration.ElasticsearchConfiguration.config|
	When these properties
		|osgi.module.configurations|operationMode="EMBEDDED" clientTransportIgnoreClusterName="false" indexNamePrefix="liferay-" httpCORSConfigurations="" additionalConfigurations="" httpCORSAllowOrigin="/https?://localhost(:[0-9]+)?/" networkBindHost="" transportTcpPort="" bootstrapMlockAll="false" networkPublishHost="" overrideTypeMappings="" clientTransportSniff="true" additionalIndexConfigurations="" retryOnConflict="5" httpCORSEnabled="true" clientTransportNodesSamplerInterval="5s" additionalTypeMappings="" logExceptionsOnly="true" httpEnabled="true" networkHost="" transportAddresses="localhost:9300" clusterName="LiferayElasticsearchCluster1" discoveryZenPingUnicastHostsPort="9300-9400"|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://localhost:9200|
	Then Elasticsearch view Cluster Status
		|clusterStatus|"cluster_name" : "LiferayElasticsearchCluster1"|
Scenario: Assert Index On Startup Via Remote
Priority: 5
##########################################################
The Poshi description element is not supported in the readable syntax. Please update this test.
##########################################################
	When these properties
		|remote.elasticsearch.enabled|true|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Users
		|portlet|Users and Organizations|
	Then User view CP
		|userEmailAddress|test@liferay.com|
		|userFirstName|Test|
		|userLastName|Test|
		|userScreenName|test|
Scenario: Assert System Settings Propogate To Module
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|Elasticsearch#AssertSystemSettingsPropogateToModule|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|System Settings|
	And SystemSettings goto Category
		|category|Foundation|
	And SystemSettings view Configuration
		|configurationName|Elasticsearch|
	And SystemSettings edit Text Area Setting
		|settingName|clusterName|
		|settingValue|LiferayElasticsearchCluster1|
	And SystemSettings save Configuration
	Then Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://localhost:9200|